1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,445
Two laws follow.

2
00:00:01,445 --> 00:00:10,078
The law of dominance: in a hybrid only the dominant allele shows, while the recessive stays hidden but unchanged.

3
00:00:10,078 --> 00:00:19,101
And the law of segregation, or purity of gametes: the two alleles separate when gametes form, so each gamete gets only one.

4
00:00:19,101 --> 00:00:21,158
A gamete is never hybrid.

5
00:00:21,158 --> 00:00:28,854
The physical reason is anaphase one of meiosis, when the two homologous chromosomes go to opposite poles.

